<?php
defined('BASEPATH') or exit('No direct script access allowed');

/**
 * Service_entitlement_pricing — Phase D of the Student Entitlements roadmap.
 *
 * ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
 *  WHY THIS EXISTS
 * ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
 *  Baseline §0A.4 path #3: Transport / Hostel module fees are generated by
 *  Fee_lifecycle::createModuleFee(), whose discount source is listed as
 *  literally "None". A student holding a transport-scoped concession is
 *  billed the full fare, because that generator has never consulted any
 *  concession source at all. That is gap G4 — "Family A, but not
 *  chart/concession-aware ... exactly what Phase D unifies".
 *
 *  This class is the pricing primitive that closes it: given one service
 *  demand, return the net after any entitlement that legitimately applies
 *  to it.
 *
 * ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
 *  WHAT IT DELIBERATELY DOES NOT DO
 * ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
 *  • It does not read `studentConcessions`. Service pricing is entitlement-
 *    native from the start — there is no legacy service-concession source to
 *    be compatible with, precisely because path #3 never had one. Adding a
 *    legacy read here would invent a bridge to a thing that does not exist.
 *  • It does not write. Ever. Pricing is a pure function of (student,
 *    service, period, gross); the caller owns the write.
 *  • It does not re-implement entitlement READING or MATCHING. It consumes
 *    Fee_entitlement_reader (Phase C, frozen) through its public API, so the
 *    query shape, the effective-window logic and invariant I3 all stay in
 *    exactly one place.
 *
 * ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
 *  KNOWN, ACCEPTED DUPLICATION (operator decision, 2026-08-08)
 * ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
 *  The accumulation rule below — fullExempt wins outright; percent and fixed
 *  otherwise accumulate; net floors at zero — also exists inside
 *  Fee_generation_service::_applyDeductions(), which is FROZEN Phase C code
 *  and must not be edited. The operator explicitly chose to accept this
 *  temporary duplication rather than break the Phase C freeze, on the
 *  condition that nothing is committed until the whole module is certified.
 *
 *  CERTIFICATION CLEANUP ITEM: during the final consolidation stage, this
 *  primitive and _applyDeductions() should converge on a single canonical
 *  implementation — but ONLY if that refactor is behaviour-preserving and
 *  fully re-verified. Until then, any change to the rule here MUST be
 *  mirrored there, and vice versa. Keeping the two in sync is a release
 *  gate, not a nicety: they price real money.
 */
class Service_entitlement_pricing
{
    /** @var object|null Fee_entitlement_reader (Phase C, frozen — consumed read-only) */
    private $reader;

    private string $schoolId = '';
    private string $session  = '';

    public function init($reader, string $schoolId, string $session): void
    {
        $this->reader   = $reader;
        $this->schoolId = $schoolId;
        $this->session  = $session;
    }

    /**
     * Net payable for ONE service demand after applicable entitlements.
     *
     * Invariant I3 is enforced inside Fee_entitlement_reader::appliesTo():
     * an entitlement scoped 'all' can never reach a service category, so only
     * a deliberately service-scoped entitlement ('category:transport',
     * 'head:<bus fee>') can discount a bus or hostel charge. A blanket
     * "20% off everything" does NOT cut the fare — which is the behaviour
     * every mature K-12 ERP implements, because service charges recover a
     * real per-student cost (a seat, a bed, a meal) rather than tuition
     * margin.
     *
     * Fails OPEN to the gross amount on any error: a pricing failure must
     * never silently under-bill. Under-charging is a revenue loss that no
     * report surfaces; billing the full configured amount is the safe
     * default, and the failure is logged for follow-up.
     *
     * @param string $serviceCategory lowercase module category ('transport'|'hostel'|…)
     * @return array{net: float, deduction: float, applied: int}
     */
    /**
     * ══ TRN-CONC-PERIOD-1 · OPEN DEFECT, DELIBERATELY NOT FIXED HERE ══
     *
     * createModuleFee() writes ONE demand per academic session and stamps it
     * with the session's FIRST month — periodKey '2026-04' — whatever month
     * the service actually starts in. appliesTo() reads that as a real month
     * and refuses any entitlement effective after it. For a service fee that
     * silently voids every concession granted after April. Reproduced at
     * runtime, same student, same route, same ACTIVE 50% category:transport
     * concession:
     *     effectiveFrom 2026-04-01  ->  50% applied, net 4,000
     *     effectiveFrom 2026-08-30  ->  nothing applied, net 8,000
     * The operator sees "Entitlement recorded." and the parent is billed in
     * full — no error, nothing in the logs.
     *
     * A FIX WAS WRITTEN AND REVERTED. Widening the test to "effective at any
     * point in the session" made a FUTURE-dated concession apply immediately
     * and made a concession scheduled to end in September still discount a
     * November period — both caught by ServiceEntitlementPricingUatTest,
     * which encodes those windows on purpose. Trading a silent under-charge
     * for a silent over-charge is not a fix.
     *
     * WHY IT IS LEFT OPEN. A single session-scoped demand cannot express a
     * concession that starts part-way through the period it covers. Deciding
     * what a mid-session transport concession should cost — the whole session,
     * or only the months from its effective date — is a PRICING decision, not
     * an engineering detail, and it changes real money for real families.
     * Recorded for that decision rather than guessed at.
     */

    /**
     * ══ PER-MONTH PRICING · THE INTERSECTION, NOT A WIDENED WINDOW ═════════
     *
     * THE PROBLEM THIS SOLVES (TRN-CONC-PERIOD-1). A service demand is stamped
     * with the SESSION's first month whatever month service starts, and
     * appliesTo() reads that key as a real month. A concession effective from
     * December was therefore compared against April and refused — silently, so
     * the operator saw "Entitlement recorded." and the parent paid in full.
     *
     * THE APPROACH THAT WAS TRIED AND REVERTED. Widening the test to "effective
     * anywhere in the session" made FUTURE-dated concessions apply immediately
     * and kept a concession scheduled to end in September discounting a
     * November period. Trading a silent under-charge for a silent over-charge
     * is not a fix, and ServiceEntitlementPricingUatTest encodes those windows
     * deliberately.
     *
     * WHAT THIS DOES INSTEAD. It asks appliesTo() the SAME question it has
     * always answered, once per month the student actually had the service:
     *
     *      SERVICE ACTIVE MONTHS  ∩  CONCESSION VALID MONTHS  =  DISCOUNTED
     *
     * Every key passed in is a REAL month, so effective-from and effective-to
     * are compared against the period they describe. A December concession
     * discounts December to March and nothing earlier; a concession that
     * expired in September discounts nothing after it. appliesTo() is
     * UNCHANGED — including invariant I3, which still decides inside it that a
     * blanket scope:'all' concession may never reach a service category.
     *
     * FIXED AMOUNTS ARE NOT MULTIPLIED. A percent applies to each month's own
     * fare, and fullExempt zeroes the months it covers — both are unambiguous
     * per month. A FIXED amount is deducted ONCE, on the first month it
     * applies to, because that is what it has always meant against a single
     * demand: "Rs 500 off this charge", not "Rs 500 off every month". Changing
     * that silently would reprice existing fixed concessions twelve-fold.
     *
     * @param array<string, float> $monthlyFares periodKey => fare for that month
     * @return array{net: float, deduction: float, applied: int, gross: float,
     *               months: array<string, array{gross: float, deduction: float}>}
     */
    public function priceForPeriods(
        string $studentId,
        string $serviceCategory,
        string $feeHead,
        array  $monthlyFares,
        string $feeHeadRef = ''
    ): array {
        $gross = round(array_sum($monthlyFares), 2);
        $none  = ['net' => $gross, 'deduction' => 0.0, 'applied' => 0,
                  'gross' => $gross, 'months' => []];

        if ($this->reader === null || $studentId === '' || $gross <= 0) {
            return $none;
        }

        try {
            $ents = $this->reader->activeConcessionsForStudent($this->schoolId, $studentId, $this->session);
            if (empty($ents)) return $none;

            $totalDeduction = 0.0;
            $appliedCount   = 0;
            $months         = [];
            // A fixed-amount entitlement may only be taken once across the
            // whole demand — keyed so two different fixed concessions each
            // still get their one turn.
            $fixedTaken = [];

            foreach ($monthlyFares as $periodKey => $fare) {
                $fare      = round((float) $fare, 2);
                $monthDed  = 0.0;
                $exempt    = false;

                foreach ($ents as $i => $e) {
                    if (!$this->reader->appliesTo($e, (string) $periodKey, '', $feeHead, $serviceCategory, $feeHeadRef)) {
                        continue;
                    }
                    $appliedCount++;

                    $type  = $this->reader->deductionType($e);
                    $value = $this->reader->deductionValue($e);

                    if ($type === 'fullExempt') { $exempt = true; break; }
                    if ($type === 'percent')    { $monthDed += $fare * ($value / 100.0); }
                    if ($type === 'fixed' && empty($fixedTaken[$i])) {
                        $monthDed += $value;
                        $fixedTaken[$i] = true;
                    }
                }

                if ($exempt)            $monthDed = $fare;
                if ($monthDed > $fare)  $monthDed = $fare;   // never below zero for the month

                $totalDeduction += $monthDed;
                $months[(string) $periodKey] = ['gross' => $fare, 'deduction' => round($monthDed, 2)];
            }

            $totalDeduction = round(min($totalDeduction, $gross), 2);

            return [
                'net'       => round($gross - $totalDeduction, 2),
                'deduction' => $totalDeduction,
                'applied'   => $appliedCount,
                'gross'     => $gross,
                'months'    => $months,
            ];
        } catch (\Throwable $e) {
            // Fails OPEN to gross, exactly as priceFor() does: a pricing
            // failure must never silently under-bill.
            log_message('error', "SERVICE_PRICING_PERIODS_FAILED [{$studentId}/{$serviceCategory}] — billing GROSS: " . $e->getMessage());
            return $none;
        }
    }

    public function priceFor(
        string $studentId,
        string $serviceCategory,
        string $feeHead,
        string $periodKey,
        float  $gross,
        string $feeHeadRef = ''
    ): array {
        $none = ['net' => round($gross, 2), 'deduction' => 0.0, 'applied' => 0];

        if ($this->reader === null || $studentId === '' || $gross <= 0) {
            return $none;
        }

        try {
            $ents = $this->reader->activeConcessionsForStudent($this->schoolId, $studentId, $this->session);
            if (empty($ents)) return $none;

            // ── The accumulation rule (see the duplication note above) ──
            $deduction  = 0.0;
            $applied    = 0;
            $fullExempt = false;
            foreach ($ents as $e) {
                // feeHeadId is '' for module fees — createModuleFee does not
                // assign one — so a legacy 'head:<name>'-scoped entitlement
                // matches by NAME via the reader's documented fallback.
                //
                // ── DEC-011 (2026-08-18) — FORWARD THE REGISTRY REF ──────────
                // The ref was NOT forwarded here, which is the DEC-009 defect
                // in the service path: `appliesTo()` was called with five
                // arguments, so its FIRST match tier (feeHeadRef) could never
                // fire. With feeHeadId also passed as '', a `head:FH_…`
                // entitlement — the ONLY shape the F-3 picker can now emit —
                // fell through all three tiers and matched nothing. A student
                // holding an approved transport concession would have been
                // billed the full fare, silently, exactly as STU0184 was on
                // the tuition path.
                //
                // Inert today (USE_ENTITLEMENT_SERVICE_PRICING is false and NOT
                // granted to any tenant); fixed now so Phase D does not
                // activate a known silent overcharge. The ref comes from the
                // M5 registry stamp createModuleFee already resolves, so no
                // new lookup and no new failure mode is introduced.
                if (!$this->reader->appliesTo($e, $periodKey, '', $feeHead, $serviceCategory, $feeHeadRef)) continue;
                $applied++;
                $type  = $this->reader->deductionType($e);
                $value = $this->reader->deductionValue($e);
                if ($type === 'fullExempt') { $fullExempt = true; break; }
                if ($type === 'percent')    $deduction += $gross * ($value / 100.0);
                if ($type === 'fixed')      $deduction += $value;
            }

            if ($fullExempt) {
                return ['net' => 0.0, 'deduction' => round($gross, 2), 'applied' => $applied];
            }

            // ── STACK-1 (service path) · CONCESSIONS BEYOND THE CHARGE ─────
            //
            // The same clamp, and the same silence, that STACK-1 closed on the
            // tuition path in Fee_generation_service::_applyDeductions(). It was
            // fixed there and missed here, which is only visible once this path
            // is actually exercised.
            //
            // Stacking is legitimate — a sibling discount and a transport
            // scholarship are separate awards. What must not be silent is the
            // total going PAST the fare: the family is correctly billed zero, so
            // nothing looks wrong, while the surplus grant is recorded nowhere
            // and revoking one of two overlapping grants appears to do nothing.
            //
            // `deduction` must stay the CLAMPED figure below so that
            // gross - deduction == net holds for every reader; that is exactly
            // why the excess has to be reported rather than stored.
            if ($deduction > $gross + 0.005) {
                log_message('error', sprintf(
                    'ACC_CONCESSION_EXCEEDS_CHARGE student=[%s] service=[%s] feeHead=[%s] '
                    . 'period=[%s] gross=[%.2f] granted=[%.2f] applied=[%.2f] excess=[%.2f] '
                    . 'rules=[%d] — the concessions on this service charge total MORE than '
                    . 'the charge. The family is billed 0, which is correct, but the demand '
                    . 'can only record the clamped discount, so the surplus grant is '
                    . 'invisible and revoking one of the overlapping grants will not change '
                    . 'the bill.',
                    $studentId, $serviceCategory, $feeHead, $periodKey,
                    $gross, $deduction, $gross, $deduction - $gross, $applied
                ));
            }

            $net = max(0.0, round($gross - $deduction, 2));
            return [
                'net'       => $net,
                'deduction' => round($gross - $net, 2),
                'applied'   => $applied,
            ];
        } catch (\Throwable $e) {
            log_message('error',
                'SERVICE_ENTITLEMENT_PRICING_FAILED student=[' . $studentId . '] service=['
                . $serviceCategory . '] — billing GROSS ' . $gross . ': ' . $e->getMessage());
            return $none;
        }
    }
}
